      (c)   Most candidates could define field water capacity, some candidates, however, referred to liquid that
            remains in the soil instead of water.
            Most candidates failed to give a proper definition of permanent wilting point as they referred to it as the point
            where plants wilt permanently.

            Answer
            Field water capacity is the amount of water that remains in the soil when the gravitational water has
            drained out of it;
            Wilting point is the minimum amount of water that plants require to stop them from wilting.

3 (a) Most     candidates     could     score     one     mark     for     the     plant     bending     towards     light,     however,     the     majority
            referred  to  plant  leaves  instead  of  seedling/shoot.   A  few  candidates  could  not  mention  auxin  as  the
            hormone that causes changes in growth.
            Answer
            plant growth substance/auxin, is made in the shoot tip;
            move / diffuse to shaded side/away from light;
            more auxin accumulates in shaded side;
            cells grow faster / more rapidly / elongated / divide more rapidly;
            seedling / shoot grows (bends) toward the light;

      (b)   Most candidates lost this mark as they referred to the response as “phototropism” only and failed to
            mention “positive”.
            Answer
            Positive phototropism;

      (c)   Well answered.
            Answer
            Auxin;

      (d)   Most candidates scored a mark for stem growth by cell elongation but failed to mention the other
            roles of auxin. Some referred to the roles of synthetic auxin.
            Answer
            Control the direction in which shoots and roots grow;
            Promote stem growth by cell elongation;
            Inhibits the growth of side shoots near the tip of the main stem;
            Inhibits root growth;
            Promotes root branching/fruit development;

