5 (a) The majority of candidates could explain what is meant by a vegetable crop.
                    Answer
                    A vegetable crop is a crop that is grown for its edible leaves, roots, stem, fruit or seed, which are used as
                    food for humans;

          (b)       Most candidates gave the correct answer for the first part of the question, the year, but failed to give
                    a proper reason.  Some candidates provided the range instead of a single year.
                    Answer
                    Year 2018; Rapid increase in yield from 12.6 to 14;

          (c)       Most candidates scored this mark.
                    Answer
                    Yield improved progressively more from 2018 to 2020;

          (d)       This  question  was  poorly  answered.    Few  candidates  managed  to  find  the  amount  of  N  in  the  NPK
                    compound fertiliser but failed to calculate the amount of N in LAN fertiliser.
                    LAN (14):                     14/100 x 50kg = 7kg;
                                                           7kg x 3 bags of LAN = 21kg of N;
                              Mixed fertiliser:                      2/9 x 15 = 3.33%;
                                                                             3.33/100 x 50kg = 1.665kg;
                                                                             1.665kg x 3 bags = 4.995kg of N;
                              Total N = 21kg + 4.995kg = 25.995kg or 26kg of N;

