            5.  (diffusion) through alveolar wall / squamous epithelial cells;
            6.  (diffusion) through endothelium / capillary wall;
            7.  oxygen binds with haemoglobin; AVP

      (c)   In this question candidates had to look at the change in the appearance of the alveoli in Fig. 4.2 A
            and B.  Then they had to explain how COPD causes this change and what effect this has on gaseous
            exchange.  Some candidates did not know what COPD is.
            Marking points 1 – 3 are focusing on the fact that there are fewer alveoli.
            Marking points 4 – 5 are focusing on the fact that the alveoli are less elastic.
            Some candidates referred to any facts relating to COPD, and not only to the role of emphysema in COPD.
            Many candidates thought that COPD causes emphysema and chronic bronchitis.

            1.  gas exchange less efficient / less gases diffuse / less oxygen diffuses into blood;
            2.  due to smaller surface area for exchange/diffusion; AW
            3.  fewer alveoli / ref. to emphysema / walls of alveoli collapse;
            4.  alveoli less elastic;
            5.  which makes it difficult to expel air from lungs / alveoli cannot / find it difficult , to stretch and recoil during
             breathing;
            6.  concentration gradient less steep;
            7.  which decreases rate of diffusion;
Question 5

      (a)   Many candidates described the process of making alginate beads, which is not an explanation of
            what is meant by immobilizing enzymes.
            Enzyme molecules are confined to / attached to / trapped in / ref. to unable to move;
            an inactive / inert / insoluble material / (solid) support / (alginate) beads;

      (b)   All enzymes can be reused.  However, it is just easier to do so when they are kept separately from the
            solutions in which the substrates are found on which they must act.  If enzymes are in solution when
            they are catalysing the reaction, the enzymes must be separated from the product solution, which takes time
           Separation of the product is easier / product does not contain enzymes / product not contaminated by enzymes;
           Enzyme is less likely to denature / enzyme is more stable / more tolerant to temperature / pH changes;
           candidates referred to high and low temperatures and pH
           Enzymes can easily be reused / immediately available for reuse;
           more cost effective as enzymes do not need to be replaced / no enzymes are lost;

      (c) (i)     This question was answered fairly well by many candidates.  Some unfortunately lost marks for
                  not writing the units in which the product concentration was measured.
                  All results for product are approximately double / product increases;
                  The average product is approximately double;
                  Allow reference to correct numbers with units;
                  Allow answers using substrate halving as enzyme doubles; AW

       (ii) Many candidates earned marking point 1 by stating that more repeats are needed for greater accuracy.
                  Very few mentioned that the range of different enzyme concentrations should be extended
                  1. ref. to more repeats (to calculate an average);
                  2. extend range of enzyme concentrations further / example of range – at least 3 more (0.6 , 0.8, 1.0) /
                  use more different enzyme concentrations;

      (d)   Most candidates referred to the production of lactose free milk.  It is important to note that only naming
            an industry, e.g. producing milk, or diary industry is not enough to gain a mark.  It must be clear for
            what purpose the immobilised enzymes are used.
            Note: it must be lactose free milk and not lactase free milk.
            Production      of      lactose      free      milk      /      biofuels      /      (high)      fructose      corn      syrup      /      refinement      of      beers      (breweries)      /
            processing   of   fibres   in   textile   industry   /   assist   in   pulping   of   wood   for   paper   production   /   cheese   production   /
            clearing fruit juice / for diagnostic purposes / developing new medicines / pre-digesting baby food; AVP

          Answer
          A - axis correctly labelled: x-axis = temp. in °C, y-axis = absorp. in a.u.;
          S - Shape of graph – must be J-curve/exponential growth;
























(ii) The question was well answered although a few candidates could not describe the relationship
          between temperature and the permeability of cell membranes. Candidates mentioned direct
          proportion which has a different meaning.
          Answer
          Any one from:
          as temperature increases, absorption increases / ORA;
          at higher temperatures cell membranes become more permeable/ ORA;
(iii) The stronger candidates stated two factors other than the factors listed and included in the
          statement of the question.
          The most common error was that some candidates stated light instead of light intensity, water potential
          instead of the pH of water.
          Answer
          Any two from:
          -  (test-tubes) kept at same light intensity;
          -  water has the same pH/ use distilled water;
          - same position of discs specified;
          OVP;
(iv) Many candidates referred to ‘repeating the experiments’.  However, they failed to add to calculate
          the average. Some candidates also referred to additional readings which does not mean the
          same as experiments. In addition, the candidates misunderstood the question and could not give
          any other correct answer.
          Answer
          1.  wash the discs before adding to the test tubes;
          2.  Repeat the experiment + take average values;                         reject repeat alone
          3.   Measure at extreme low and high temperatures;
          AVP;
          Reject - leave in water for longer time
